This plugin contains content derived from ThariqS/html-effectiveness
(https://github.com/ThariqS/html-effectiveness, commit 5d64f68 at time
of port), authored by Thariq Shihipar, moved here from the retired
workbench plugin in deprecated 0.5.0:

  - skills/crafting-html/SKILL.md (original work, not derived)
  - skills/crafting-html/references/*.html (verbatim bodies except
      U+2014 and U+2013 replaced with project-lint-compliant
      punctuation; no semantic content changed)

At commit 5d64f68 the upstream repository declared no license (GitHub
API reported license: null, and the repo had no LICENSE file). Content
is included under the upstream author's public publishing intent (the
repository is the published gallery referenced from Thariq Shihipar's
blog post on HTML effectiveness, with the explicit invitation
"you can see a bunch here: https://thariqs.github.io/html-effectiveness").
All rights to the original text remain with Thariq Shihipar.

Upstream licensed the repository after the port. Commit cbc9cfc
(2026-05-15) added an MIT LICENSE, "Copyright (c) 2026 Anthropic PBC".
Commit 67ed672 (2026-05-18) switched it to Apache-2.0; it merged as
0e8d447 (PR #5, "Switch to Apache-2.0"). The appendix of the Apache
LICENSE names "Copyright 2026 Anthropic PBC". Upstream HTML files
since then open with a comment that holds "Copyright 2026 Anthropic
PBC" and "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0".

The files shipped here come from 5d64f68, before both changes, so the
no-license shape above still fits them. The archive is frozen, so no
refresh at a licensed upstream commit is planned.

Adaptations to the crafting-html references (the punctuation
substitution) are mechanical and add no original authorship.
